<title>USA: Lason to offer more shares in IPO.</title>
<headline>Lason to offer more shares in IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lason Holdings Inc increased the number of shares it will offer in its proposed initial public offering, according to a regulatory filing.</p>
<p>The company will offer 3.0 million, up from its initial estimate of 2.7 million shares. The estimated price range of $14.50 to $16.50 a share remains the same.</p>
<p>The offering will be lead managed by Robertson Stephens.  </p>
<p>Lason offers integrated outsourcing services for records and document management. Analysts say the deal could be one of the hottest initial public offerings this week.</p>
<p>-- J. Westhoven, Wall Street Desk (212) 859-1881</p>
</text>
